  "title": "Hürrem Sultan",
  "summary": "Hürrem Sultan, known in Europe as Roxelana, was an enslaved concubine from Ruthenia who rose to become the chief consort and legally wedded wife of Ottoman Sultan Suleiman the Magnificent. Breaking centuries of imperial precedent, she exercised extraordinary political and diplomatic authority, conducted international correspondence, patronized extensive architectural complexes, and inaugurated the influential era known as the Sultanate of Women.",
